 "final_result": "NaCl band-structure workflow completed successfully.\n\nMaterials Project ID: mp-22862 (rock salt NaCl, Fm-3m #225)\nAtom count: 2 before and after primitive-cell reduction (already primitive)\n\nWorkflow outline:\n1. Fetched NaCl CIF from Materials Project (mp-22862), reduced to primitive cell via chem_llm.kpath (nat=2, unchanged).\n2. generate_structures.py: wrote 51 structures (000-050) with thermal displacements at 300 K (NaCl is stable at room temperature, melting point ~1074 K). Na RMS=0.074 A, Cl RMS=0.067 A, strain ~0.1%.\n3. Fetched pseudopotentials: Na (z_valence=9, sr, 44 Ha) and Cl (z_valence=7, sr, 29 Ha). Total electrons=16, occupied bands=8.\n4. setup_jobs.py: created 51 calculation directories with pw.in (SCF, ecutwfc=88 Ry, ecutrho=352 Ry, kpts 8x8x8), bands.in (NSCF, nbnd=20), bands_post.in (bands.x, lsym=.false.).\n5. run_espresso_workflow on calculations/000: success=true, all 3 steps completed (scf=3.8s, bands_scf=15.5s, bands_post=2.8s).\n6. plot_bands.py: plotted band structure aligned to VBM, saved to calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.\n\nASE functions used: ase.io.read/write for CIF I/O, ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in for QE input files, ase.Atoms for structure representation.\n\nBand gap obtained: 5.04 eV (VBM=1.215 eV, CBM=6.255 eV). This is close to the Materials Project value of 5.00 eV.\n\nScientific assumptions:\n- Scalar-relativistic pseudopotentials (Na Z=11, Cl Z=17, both < 54)\n- occupations='fixed' (NaCl is an insulator)\n- nspin=1 (non-magnetic)\n- 300 K thermal displacements (NaCl stable at room temperature)\n\nAll three scripts (generate_structures.py, setup_jobs.py, plot_bands.py) ran with returncode 0. No pymatgen imports. run_espresso_workflow returned success: true for calculations/000.",
